## 8. CUSTOMER ORDER MANAGEMENT — COMPLETE WORKFLOW

This is a critical feature.

Inspect and improve the entire customer ordering workflow.

When a customer successfully places an order:

1. Generate a unique order number automatically.
2. Save the order permanently in Firestore.
3. Record the customer ID.
4. Record the supplier ID.
5. Record the relevant product IDs.
6. Record product quantities.
7. Record agreed prices and totals.
8. Record the customer's delivery information.
9. Record the customer's contact phone number.
10. Record the supplier's contact phone number.
11. Record order creation date and time.
12. Record the initial order status.

The generated order number must be unique and must never be reused.

Example format:

TE-2026-000001

Use a collision-resistant generation method. Do not rely on simple frontend counters.

### 8.1 Customer order confirmation

After successfully placing an order:

- Show a successful order confirmation screen.
- Display the generated order number.
- Display the order summary.
- Display the supplier's business/contact phone number where authorized.
- Display the customer's own contact number.
- Show the current order status.
- Provide a way to open order details.
- Send a persistent notification confirming that the order was received.

Do not tell the customer an order was placed if the database transaction failed.

### 8.2 Supplier order notification

When a customer places an order:

- Notify the relevant supplier immediately.
- Display the new order in the supplier dashboard.
- Display the unique order number.
- Display the customer's name and contact phone number where necessary for fulfilling that order.
- Display the customer's delivery details.
- Display the ordered products and quantities.
- Display the agreed supplier payment information according to existing business rules.
- Provide order acceptance and management actions.

Suppliers must not see other suppliers' private customer orders.

### 8.3 Supplier acceptance

When the supplier accepts an order:

- Update the order status in Firestore.
- Record supplier acceptance date and time.
- Notify the customer.
- Show the updated status in both dashboards.

If the supplier rejects or cannot fulfil an order, record the reason and notify the customer and Admin.

### 8.4 Delivery confirmation by supplier

When the supplier has delivered the order:

Provide a clear action:

"Mark Order as Delivered"

Before accepting this action:

- Verify the supplier is authorized for this order.
- Verify the current order status.
- Record delivery date and time.
- Record the supplier's delivery confirmation.
- Update the order status to awaiting customer confirmation.

IMPORTANT:

Supplier delivery confirmation must NOT automatically mark the order as fully completed.

The customer must be given an opportunity to confirm actual receipt.

### 8.5 Customer delivery confirmation

When the supplier marks an order as delivered:

Immediately send the customer a persistent notification.

Example notification:

"Your order TE-2026-000001 has been marked as delivered by the supplier. Please confirm whether you have received your order."

Display two appropriate actions:

- "Confirm I Received My Order"
- "Report a Delivery Problem"

When the customer confirms receipt:

- Verify that the customer owns the order.
- Verify the order is awaiting customer confirmation.
- Record the customer's confirmation.
- Record confirmation date and time.
- Update the order status to COMPLETED.
- Notify the supplier.
- Notify Admin.
- Preserve the complete order history.

If the customer reports a problem:

- Do not automatically complete the order.
- Create a delivery dispute or support case.
- Notify Admin and the supplier.
- Preserve all relevant records.
- Allow Admin to investigate and resolve the issue.

Do not allow unauthorized users to confirm delivery.

### 8.6 Order status system

Implement a consistent order state machine using the existing architecture.

Recommended statuses:

- PENDING
- ACCEPTED
- PROCESSING
- READY_FOR_DELIVERY
- OUT_FOR_DELIVERY
- AWAITING_CUSTOMER_CONFIRMATION
- COMPLETED
- REJECTED
- CANCELLED
- DELIVERY_DISPUTE

Only allow valid status transitions.

Record:
- Previous status.
- New status.
- User performing the action.
- User role.
- Timestamp.
- Optional reason or notes.

Do not allow customers, suppliers or administrators to bypass authorization rules.

